1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:00,820
Ohhh!

2
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:05,590
Meet oa and ow — two friends who both make the long O sound...

3
00:00:05,980 --> 00:00:06,480
oooh!

4
00:00:07,560 --> 00:00:09,180
You hear that sound in boat...

5
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:10,670
and in snow!

6
00:00:11,560 --> 00:00:12,640
Same sound...

7
00:00:12,740 --> 00:00:13,640
different spelling!

8
00:00:14,760 --> 00:00:16,780
But how do we know which one to use?

9
00:00:18,180 --> 00:00:19,980
Here's an easy way to remember!

10
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:22,060
Think of a little boat.

11
00:00:22,900 --> 00:00:25,830
oa loves to sail in the middle of a word.

12
00:00:26,140 --> 00:00:28,040
b-o-a-t…

13
00:00:28,040 --> 00:00:28,600
boat!

14
00:00:29,740 --> 00:00:31,880
Now think of a big wave.

15
00:00:32,660 --> 00:00:34,380
ow loves the end of a word.

16
00:00:35,260 --> 00:00:36,960
s-n-o-w...

17
00:00:37,760 --> 00:00:38,060
snow!

18
00:00:39,660 --> 00:00:41,000
Let's try some more words!

19
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:42,900
Coat...

20
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:43,380
goat...

21
00:00:44,120 --> 00:00:44,400
toast...

22
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:46,760
oa is in the middle.

23
00:00:48,060 --> 00:00:48,780
Grow...

24
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:49,520
blow...

25
00:00:50,060 --> 00:00:50,560
yellow...

26
00:00:51,280 --> 00:00:52,800
ow is at the end!

27
00:00:54,180 --> 00:00:55,840
Now it's your turn!

28
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:57,100
Which one goes here?

29
00:00:58,120 --> 00:00:58,520
road...

30
00:00:59,260 --> 00:01:00,780
oa or ow?

31
00:01:02,060 --> 00:01:04,340
It's oa — because it's in the middle!

32
00:01:05,480 --> 00:01:09,420
oa sails in the middle, and ow rolls to the end.

33
00:01:10,360 --> 00:01:11,020
Easy, right?

34
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:16,800
Get the English Learning app — where kids learn to read the fun way!
